 "kind": "knowledge",
 "definition": "A measure of how well a material resists being permanently dented by a hard point pressed into it, found with tests such as Brinell, Vickers and Rockwell.",
 "description": {
  "text": "Indentation hardness tests, used in mechanical engineering, measure a material's resistance to deformation by pressing into it until an impression forms. They can be done at macroscopic or microscopic scale.",
